# Source-assisted Sketch layout attribution

Selected source release: Excalidraw0.18.1, official commit `a2ec2889babf7d2295469c6d90ebe77fae57df84`, MIT. Source provenance metadata is preserved unchanged at the proposed app path `results/layout-followup/correction/frozen/source-provenance.json.snapshot`. The exact original license is `results/layout-followup/correction/frozen/original/LICENSE.snapshot.snapshot` (SHA `1352d204fdb90d5e482c13139d848bc2c9300a9a7de358a0a558a23e72d0d8be`). All eight complete selected files retain their copyright/license headers and original acquisition URLs/digests.

Verification composes seven unchanged original slices: complete alignment and distribution helper bodies; `getMaximumGroups`; `getCommonBounds` and `getCommonBoundingBox`; complete `mutateElement` and `newElementWith` bodies. These supply eight declarations across five source units. ActionAlign and ActionDistribute are retained for action/key/selection semantics but are not full original UI execution. Node TypeScript erasure removes module syntax/types; source slice and compiled digests are recorded. Original bodies are not edited. Only verification imports or evaluates these files; live client/runtime never loads them.

Explicitly owned dependency adapters are unrotated direct rectangle/diamond/ellipse/text bounds or actual two-point line/freehand extrema; clock/random, undefined scene lookup, excluded elbow predicate, and unbound-text/binding no-ops. There is no original full bounds/renderer, frame membership, binding, text layout, rotation or GUI claim. Runtime layout is source-assisted new implementation and is not represented as independently clean-room code. Exact historical failed comparisons and the independent correction acceptance are retained separately; MIT attribution does not imply endorsement or full compatibility.
